<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Use This Soil Calculator</h2>
    <p>Filling raised beds or topdressing lawns requires calculating total soil volume before buying bulk soil or bagged topsoil. Use this tool with simple steps:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Planter Shape:</strong> Select rectangular for standard 4x8 ft raised garden beds or circular for round containers.</li>
        <li><strong>Bed Dimensions:</strong> Enter garden length, width, or planter diameter in feet or meters.</li>
        <li><strong>Soil Depth:</strong> Enter soil depth in inches or centimeters (standard raised vegetable beds require 10 to 12 inches of soil).</li>
        <li><strong>Soil Bag Size:</strong> Select bag size (topsoil commonly comes in 0.75 cu ft bags, while potting mix comes in 1.5 cu ft bags).</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>Soil Volume Formulas & Mix Ratio Benchmarks</h2>
    <p>Soil volume calculations use three-dimensional cubic measurement formulas converted into cubic yards or retail bag counts:</p>
    
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #2563eb;">Volume Formula (Rectangular Beds)</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Length x Width x Depth converted to cubic yards:</p>
            <p><code>Cubic Yards = (Length x Width x (Depth / 12)) / 27</code></p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #7c3aed;">Mel's Mix Raised Bed Ratio</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Standard raised bed soil recipe recommendations:</p>
            <p><code>1/3 Peat Moss + 1/3 Vermiculite + 1/3 Mixed Compost</code></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

